{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And with the breath of Your nostrils, etc.; You blew with Your breath, etc.</b> For it is the way of the world that heat [comes] through heat: by the blast of the nostrils, which is hot, the congealed waters, [being] cold, become liquefied and turn clear; and by the breath of the mouth, which is cold, they are chilled and turn to ice. But here, by the blast of the nostrils of the Holy One, blessed be He, the waters piled up and congealed and froze; and by the blowing of the breath of His mouth the sea covered them and they sank — behold, two great miracles. Therefore it is written מי כמוך twice. And in precise books, באלים is defective yod; expound it as באלמים, as it were — that the Holy One, blessed be He, is silent like a mute person, keeping silent toward those who anger Him and extending His patience to them until they return." "<b>They piled up.</b> Cunning entered them, and they said song. And thus Onkelos translated: חכימו מיא." "<b>The deeps froze in the heart of the sea.</b> The lower two-thirds froze, and the upper third split open. For had they split open below, down to the deep, [the waters] would not have been able to come out of it. And that which is written בלב ים is like the heart placed in the body of a person: two-thirds are below it and one-third above it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:18.399437850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}